# Backend API Rules

The backend is in:

apps/api

Stack:
- NestJS
- Prisma
- PostgreSQL
- JWT auth
- class-validator DTOs

## API principles

- Backend is the source of truth.
- Never trust frontend role checks.
- Validate all inputs.
- Use transactions for orders, payments, delivery status, and stock changes.
- Keep controllers thin and services clear.
- Return clear errors.

## Auth rules

- Use JWT guard and role decorators consistently.
- Public endpoints must be intentional.
- Protected endpoints must check ownership or role.
- Delivery agents can only access assigned orders.
- Company pricing must be checked server-side.

## Database rules

- Use Prisma migrations for schema changes.
- Do not edit generated files.
- Do not change schema without explaining migration impact.
- Preserve existing demo seed accounts unless intentionally updating seed data.

## Production readiness

Avoid:
- open CORS in production
- default secrets
- health endpoints behind auth
- missing rate limits on auth
- fake payment status changes without business rules